-13. The selected toolchain must be Go 1.23 or newer, must pass the closed toolchain-identity rules in section 4.2, and must be in a Go release family the manager has tested against the `go-v1` conformance vectors. An unknown future release is not accepted merely because its version compares greater than 1.23.
-14. The fixed dependency listing must cover the root and every active dependency. Every non-standard package must resolve inside the snapshot and have empty `CgoFiles`, `CFiles`, `CXXFiles`, `MFiles`, `HFiles`, `FFiles`, `SFiles`, `SwigFiles`, `SwigCXXFiles`, and `SysoFiles`; every package, including the standard library, must have empty `SysoFiles`. Listed embedded inputs must resolve within the same trusted root as their package. Any violation fails before `go build`.
