+### 3.5 Context-selection vectors
+
+The positive vector is compiler-free. All possible main-module, vendored, and embedded inputs live below the statically excluded build root, while ordinary skill instructions remain agent-facing:
+
+```json
+{
+  "name": "build-root-excluded-from-agent-context",
+  "manifest": {
+    "schema_version": 6,
+    "build_roots": ["build"],
+    "commands": {
+      "golden-tool": {
+        "type": "build",
+        "driver": "go-v1",
+        "source_dir": "build/cmd/golden-tool"
+      }
+    },
+    "capabilities": {
+      "network": "none",
+      "filesystem": "repo",
+      "exec": "none",
+      "secrets": "none",
+      "env_read": []
+    },
+    "dependencies": {}
+  },
+  "snapshot_files": [
+    "SKILL.md",
+    "assets/prompt.md",
+    "build/go.mod",
+    "build/cmd/golden-tool/main.go",
+    "build/internal/render/render.go",
+    "build/internal/render/template.txt"
+  ],
+  "expected_context_files": ["SKILL.md", "assets/prompt.md"],
+  "expected_excluded_files": [
+    "build/go.mod",
+    "build/cmd/golden-tool/main.go",
+    "build/internal/render/render.go",
+    "build/internal/render/template.txt"
+  ],
+  "cache_hit_go_commands": [],
+  "dry_run_go_commands": []
+}
+```
+
+The negative vector fails before context selection, cache lookup, or any Go command. Root modules fail for the same reason because `.` is not a portable build root in v1.
