-5. Validate cache receipts/artifacts read-only and produce a complete hit/miss/corrupt plan.
-6. **Dry-run deletes the probe root and ends here.** A miss is reported as `would-preflight-and-build`, because dry-run deliberately does not run source-aware `go list`.
-7. For a real operation, retain the private root, add one staging tree and transaction journal, and for every cache miss in provider-first/node-command order run the fixed full-graph `go list` preflight followed by fixed `go build` against that same validated raw snapshot. Do not publish anything yet; any snapshot change aborts the operation.
